# NOTE: root-level pages (about-us, contact, request-tool, privacy-policy,
# terms-of-service, disclaimer, cookie-policy, security, gizlilik-politikasi,
# kvkk-aydinlatma-metni, kullanim-kosullari, iletisim) intentionally have NO
# clean-URL rewrite rule here. Cloudflare Pages already serves `/about-us`
# from `about-us.html` natively, and already 308-redirects `/about-us.html`
# to `/about-us`. A custom rule rewriting the clean path back to the same
# `.html` file collides with that native handling and produces an infinite
# self-redirect (`/about-us` -> 308 -> `/about-us`), which is exactly the
# 404/redirect-loop bug reported on these pages in production. Do not
# reintroduce a `/<page> /<page>.html 200` rule for a page that already has
# a same-named `.html` file — see tests/site-regressions.mjs for the guard.

# The old /tools/request/ route contains an unconfigured Formspree placeholder.
# Canonicalize it to the honest mailto-based request page instead of exposing
# a form that cannot submit successfully.
/tools/request /request-tool.html 301
/tools/request/ /request-tool.html 301

# Legacy source-tree tool URLs must never render the 404 shell.
# Preserve the complete tool suffix and move users to the canonical public namespace.
/src/tools/* /tools/:splat 301

# Two-sentence author stubs duplicated the full profiles that every article links to.
# Different target names, so this cannot loop with the native .html handling.
/author/metehan /author/metehan-cetin 301
/author/metehan/ /author/metehan-cetin 301
/author/editorial /author/novatools-editorial 301
/author/editorial/ /author/novatools-editorial 301

# Per-topic blog archives were retired (each would list one or two posts);
# the blog hub lists every published post. The archive files no longer
# exist, so this cannot collide with native .html handling.
/blog/categories /blog/ 301
/blog/categories/ /blog/ 301
/blog/categories/* /blog/ 301

# Retired 2026-11-27 (docs/research/page-audit.csv, decision D-006). The
# /guides/ cluster was template text (the same paragraph under every heading,
# "publish-ready outline and article draft" visible to readers) and the topic
# map only indexed it. Sources are deleted and every link to them removed;
# these keep old inbound links useful. Redirects run before static assets.
/guides /blog/ 301
/guides/ /blog/ 301
/guides/* /blog/ 301
/site-map/topical /categories/ 301
/site-map/topical.html /categories/ 301
/site-map/topical/ /categories/ 301

# Duplicate copies that each declared themselves canonical:
# /about (public/about.html) duplicated /about-us; the article template was an
# indexable empty page; /blog/<slug> duplicated /blog/articles/<slug>.html,
# served extensionless (its canonical).
/about /about-us 301
/about.html /about-us 301
/about/ /about-us 301
/blog/article-template /blog/ 301
/blog/article-template.html /blog/ 301
/blog/browser-based-tools-vs-desktop-software-privacy-comparison /blog/articles/browser-based-tools-vs-desktop-software-privacy-comparison 301
/blog/edit-pdf-without-adobe-acrobat-free-methods /blog/articles/edit-pdf-without-adobe-acrobat-free-methods 301
/blog/lazy-loading-images-implementation-guide-2026 /blog/articles/lazy-loading-images-implementation-guide-2026 301
/blog/pdf-financial-records /blog/articles/pdf-financial-records 301
/blog/rule-of-72-estimate-investment-doubling-time /blog/articles/rule-of-72-estimate-investment-doubling-time 301
/blog/understanding-json-web-tokens-structure-security /blog/articles/understanding-json-web-tokens-structure-security 301

# NOTE: category, blog, and guides clean URLs are likewise handled by
# Cloudflare's native `.html`-stripping behavior and intentionally have no
# rewrite rule here, for the same self-redirect-loop reason described above.

# Unsupported legacy locale-folder URLs fall back to the equivalent clean
# English route instead of creating query-locale URLs that the runtime does
# not support. Preserve the suffix so valid tools/articles keep their target.
/de / 301
/de/* /:splat 301
/fr / 301
/fr/* /:splat 301
/es / 301
/es/* /:splat 301
/pt / 301
/pt/* /:splat 301
/ru / 301
/ru/* /:splat 301
/zh / 301
/zh/* /:splat 301
/ja / 301
/ja/* /:splat 301
/ko / 301
/ko/* /:splat 301
/hi / 301
/hi/* /:splat 301
/it / 301
/it/* /:splat 301
/pl / 301
/pl/* /:splat 301
/nl / 301
/nl/* /:splat 301

# Arabic blog pages have dedicated content manifests and built routes, so no
# blanket /ar redirect is declared here. This prevents a valid Arabic article
# from being intercepted before Cloudflare Pages can serve its static asset.
# Missing routes are handled natively by Cloudflare Pages using the built 404.html.
